    "standardized_narrative": "Opening gross claims outstanding at 1 January 2021 were $1,754.7m. Analysis of the gross claims development triangle shows no material movement in estimates for underwriting years prior to 2020 (net prior-year development approximately zero), so prior year reserves are effectively flat. The 2021 underwriting year was affected by several weather-related large loss events (Hurricane Ida, Winter Storm Uri, PCS 2176) which drove 2021 claims and claims outstanding, and the 2020 results were influenced by weather events (Hurricane Laura, Hurricane Sally, PCS 2016) and incurred losses related to the Coronavirus pandemic. The syndicate purchased an Adverse Development Cover in 2020 protecting 2017 and prior casualty years (no such cover in 2021), which affected ceded spend and reinsurance recoveries for 2020.",
